=== meta ===
rule: ASSERT_REMOVED
title: a pytest mark added to the running class leaves its helper method resolved, so the method's assertion pairs with itself
origin: #487, ruling 487 (a) - a bare `pytest.mark.<name>` returns the class it decorates; #476 left the call unresolved at the commit and read the assertion as removed
=== before: tests/test_billing.py ===
import unittest

from app.billing import total


class TotalTest(unittest.TestCase):
    def _check(self, value):
        self.assertEqual(value, 78.75)

    def test_total(self):
        self._check(total([50.0, 28.75]))
=== after: tests/test_billing.py ===
import unittest

import pytest

from app.billing import total


@pytest.mark.slow
class TotalTest(unittest.TestCase):
    def _check(self, value):
        self.assertEqual(value, 78.75)

    def test_total(self):
        self._check(total([50.0, 28.75]))
